## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

- Use semantic HTML elements (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<aside>`, `<header>`).
- Every interactive element must be keyboard-navigable and have a visible focus ring.
- All images need descriptive `alt` text; decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Use `aria-label` on icon-only buttons: `<Button aria-label="Delete tenant">`.
- Ensure colour contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text, ≥ 3:1 for large text.
- Use loading skeletons / `aria-busy` during async operations — never leave the user with a blank screen.
- Form inputs must have associated `<label>` elements (via `htmlFor` or wrapping).
- Error messages must reference their field via `aria-describedby`.

## Responsive design

See `ui-responsive.mdc` for mobile-first layout rules, table patterns, and the sidebar drawer pattern.
